{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/743016-speculation-the-future-of-white-wolf-properties-in-other-media","id":743016,"title":"Speculation: The future of White Wolf properties in other media","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-30T15:17:58-07:00","id":743016,"title":"Speculation: The future of White Wolf properties in other media","content":"So we all know now that Paradox Interactive bought the White Wolf properties. Presumably that gives them the right to utilize both versions of the World of Darkness and Exalted however they see fit. Let's put aside the impact this is going to have on tabletop games to ask how you'd like to see Paradox incorporate these properties elsewhere. Given that they're a gaming company, the most reasonable relationship is video game computer game adaptations, but don't limit yourself to that.<br /> <br /> I think Vampire: The Requiem is a perfect match for Paradox's complex 4X strategy games. The systems in games like Crusader Kings and Europa Universalis seem like they'd adapt well to a Requiem adaptation about city management, where wonky decision-making like establishing rule of law, zoning territories, and assigning political positions of both ceremonial and practical import sit front and center. Plus, that balance between setting up trusted regents while you can take a torpor nap or trying to reign longer while dealing with the effects of high blood potency create a similar dynamic to the dynasty system in Paradox's existing games. I think Damnation City would be a great blueprint for a game like that.<br /> <br /> Similarly, I think Block by Bloody Block could form a great basis for a Hunter: The Vigil game crafted in the X-Com model. Give us a mix of tactical and strategic gameplay about managing a compact of hunters and expanding outward to claim your home town from the creatures of the night. Combine cautious strategic management where careful expansion, practical research and recruiting, and thorough scouting of areas is necessary to make sure you send the right team with the right equipment into each conflict with brutal, lethal tactical gameplay that that ensures every decision you make in the field could be crippling.<br /> <br /> Both seem tailor made for user-made mods as well. What ST wouldn't want to adapt their game setting into the system for players to explore?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","user":"dxanders","date":". 10-30-2015, 06:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T16:49:52-07:00","id":743235,"title":"","content":"I've said it before, and I will say it again. Mummy the Curse is perfect for Obsidian to another RPG, especially one that's a spiritual successor to Planescape: Torment. I need this. <br /> <br /> Demon: the Descent is a fairly obvious one as well. Really good synergy with and Assassin's Creed type stealth/action genre.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T17:09:22-07:00","id":743263,"title":"","content":"I haven't really explored Mummy, but what I have heard seems tremendously well suited for a CRPG. I think the multiple timelines angle in particular would create a bunch of narrative possibilities.<br /> <br /> I think a Descent game could revolutionize open world gaming. Embeds are essentially cheat codes, and you could create a really unique environment where the entire city is your adversary and the risk-reward of using your flashier powers is tied into a wanted system. They could do a lot by examining what worked and didn't work in Watchdogs. The real challenge would be finding a dev with the money, manpower, and experience to do the job right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T20:18:05-07:00","id":743596,"title":"","content":"I would want a rogue like. Not just any rogue-like, a rogue like that let's you play <i>anything</i> from all of the White Wolf games, Both CWoD, NWoD, Exalted, whatever.<br /> <br /> Obviously oversimplified, perhaps so much so that the main difference between options would be starting powers and item loadouts, but a roguelike all the same.<br /> <br /> Take for example, say uh, on the werewolf side of things, all werewolves have really good combat stats on melees and passive regen. Forsaken would be more &quot;subversive&quot; and be slightly stealthier owing to their focus as hunters and predators, where as Garou would have more beef lending to their stereotype as Gaia's Warriors. Auspices and Tribes then provide item loadouts and starting powers and so on and so forth.<br /> <br /> The style would probably be an affectionate parody and gameplay would look like the Pokemon Mystery Dungeon game series in terms of complexity.<br /> <br /> As for story, it'd be an excuse plot or a deconstruction of some sort....<br /> <br /> It's pretty unreasonable, no doubt, but the idea of this is to make a fun crossover IP for fans of WW stuff in general without having people to worry about not being represented. Think... like Smash. Something to unify the fanbase in a neat way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 10-30-2015, 11:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T20:34:56-07:00","id":743662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/743016-speculation-the-future-of-white-wolf-properties-in-other-media?p=743596#post743596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would want a rogue like. Not just any rogue-like, a rogue like that let's you play <i>anything</i> from all of the White Wolf games, Both CWoD, NWoD, Exalted, whatever.<br /> <br /> Obviously oversimplified, perhaps so much so that the main difference between options would be starting powers and item loadouts, but a roguelike all the same.<br /> <br /> Take for example, say uh, on the werewolf side of things, all werewolves have really good combat stats on melees and passive regen. Forsaken would be more &quot;subversive&quot; and be slightly stealthier owing to their focus as hunters and predators, where as Garou would have more beef lending to their stereotype as Gaia's Warriors. Auspices and Tribes then provide item loadouts and starting powers and so on and so forth.<br /> <br /> The style would probably be an affectionate parody and gameplay would look like the Pokemon Mystery Dungeon game series in terms of complexity.<br /> <br /> As for story, it'd be an excuse plot or a deconstruction of some sort....<br /> <br /> It's pretty unreasonable, no doubt, but the idea of this is to make a fun crossover IP for fans of WW stuff in general without having people to worry about not being represented. Think... like Smash. Something to unify the fanbase in a neat way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I could see this. With the Dowager being the cause and final boss (while she was looking for another Great Contagion, the other planes of existence noticed, and started pulling heroes out by the dozen to stop her by invading the Well from their sides. The drama comes from just how stressful exploring and fighting in a constantly shifting and chaotic environment controlled by Exalted's Granny Goodness actually is).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T20:38:17-07:00","id":743669,"title":"","content":"I definitely agree about Demon: The Descent having some really incredible videogame opportunities embedded in it, but I'm skeptical of them using things that aren't their One World of Darkness that seems to be all about Old World of Darkness, so I don't know the likelihood of it being made.<br /> <br /> I think it's almost a certainty that we'll be seeing a spiritual successor to Bloodlines once they've figured out their plans for this One World of Darkness. How that will look, I'm not sure, but given their interest in the IP is more than incidental, I'm certain it will turn out infinitely better than Bloodlines did. I'm not sure about what other kinds of games we might see. Probably some kind of FPS or TPS to do with Hunter types in the One World of Darkness? Who knows.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T20:44:35-07:00","id":743684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/743016-speculation-the-future-of-white-wolf-properties-in-other-media?p=743669#post743669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I definitely agree about Demon: The Descent having some really incredible videogame opportunities embedded in it, but I'm skeptical of them using things that aren't their One World of Darkness that seems to be all about Old World of Darkness, so I don't know the likelihood of it being made.<br /> <br /> I think it's almost a certainty that we'll be seeing a spiritual successor to Bloodlines once they've figured out their plans for this One World of Darkness. How that will look, I'm not sure, but given their interest in the IP is more than incidental, I'm certain it will turn out infinitely better than Bloodlines did. I'm not sure about what other kinds of games we might see. Probably some kind of FPS or TPS to do with Hunter types in the One World of Darkness? Who knows.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hadn't thought about that route for Hunter actually. The recent trend towards asynchronous multiplayer (see Evolve and the new Friday the 13th) could be a great match for the property, especially if they experiment with the idea of treating matches as a tiered micro-narrative. The Dread Powers system from Hunter could create a great way to make matches unpredictable. &quot;Okay. So we faced off against a pack of ghouls protecting this nightclub in the first round. There's probably a vampire inside. But is it the kind that can blend into the shadows or the kind that can grow claws and shrug off bullets?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","user":"dxanders","date":". 10-31-2015, 12:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T21:20:53-07:00","id":743762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/743016-speculation-the-future-of-white-wolf-properties-in-other-media?p=743596#post743596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would want a rogue like. Not just any rogue-like, a rogue like that let's you play <i>anything</i> from all of the White Wolf games, Both CWoD, NWoD, Exalted, whatever.<br /> <br /> Obviously oversimplified, perhaps so much so that the main difference between options would be starting powers and item loadouts, but a roguelike all the same.<br /> <br /> Take for example, say uh, on the werewolf side of things, all werewolves have really good combat stats on melees and passive regen. Forsaken would be more &quot;subversive&quot; and be slightly stealthier owing to their focus as hunters and predators, where as Garou would have more beef lending to their stereotype as Gaia's Warriors. Auspices and Tribes then provide item loadouts and starting powers and so on and so forth.<br /> <br /> The style would probably be an affectionate parody and gameplay would look like the Pokemon Mystery Dungeon game series in terms of complexity.<br /> <br /> As for story, it'd be an excuse plot or a deconstruction of some sort....<br /> <br /> It's pretty unreasonable, no doubt, but the idea of this is to make a fun crossover IP for fans of WW stuff in general without having people to worry about not being represented. Think... like Smash. Something to unify the fanbase in a neat way.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Shhhhh... They'll take your idea and turn it into a MOBA.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T21:35:51-07:00","id":743817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/743016-speculation-the-future-of-white-wolf-properties-in-other-media?p=743762#post743762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Shhhhh... They'll take your idea and turn it into a MOBA.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I have no fear about that; MOBA as a market are oversaturated to the point that it's not profitable to go into them at this point. It needs to stabilize alot more first before I think PI would ever want to do that.<br /> <br /> Also... we're talking about Paradox here. Niche games are their thing. MOBAs... aren't niche enough. I mean, have you <i>seen</i> what their big products are like?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T21:41:21-07:00","id":743832,"title":"","content":"Bloodlines 2.<br /> <br /> Now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T14:32:16-07:00","id":745127,"title":"","content":"Ok, pipe dream here, but picture an open-world single player game (I imagine Bethesda style, but Ubisoft style would work fine if that's more your cup of tea). You've got your big city sandbox, populated with humans, vampires, werewolves, mages, the works. You start out as a human, and the initial questline has you stumbling into the mysterious and spooky things that walk the city at night. And from there, the sky is the limit. You can play the whole game as a mortal caught up in the machinations of these monsters you just learned existed, take to hunting them, or even become one of them (obviously for splats that are tied to heritage there would have to be a sidequest where you discover your great grandpa was a werewolf, or whatever). Different quests become available or impossible for different splats, so there's a ton of replay value.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Sidenote, I think this would work better set in nWoD, just because nWoD is generally more crossover-friendly, and the modular approach lends itself nicely to sandbox play. But I definitely wouldn't say no to such a game set in oWoD either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 10-31-2015, 05:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T14:59:12-07:00","id":745180,"title":"","content":"Man people seem to quite like the mega crossover roguelike....<br /> <br /> I would have thought it would be too niche","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 10-31-2015, 06:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T19:33:04-08:00","id":748234,"title":"","content":"My idea of the perfect WtF game would be kinda of like Fallout New Vegas, but with a &quot;hunt planning&quot; feature similar to the preplanning from Payday2 for the more important quests, where you can call in favors from mortals, spirits and other being that you have helped through out the game to help crack the tougher targets of the sacred hunt, by having allies sabotage the enemy defenses, gather intelligence and leave supplies for the pack and other such things.<br /> <br /> and if you play as an Elodoth of the mastermind face, a Rahu of the tactician face or an Irraka of the scout face you get some sort of bonus to preplanning, like help costing fewer favors for the mastermind, or a discount on intelligence for the scout and a discount on more assault style assistance for the tactician. However, calling in favors requires you to help others in order to be owed those favors and some forms of help are only available if specific sorts of people or spirits owe you favors.<br /> <br /> and like I said, to make things manageable for the developers, this detailed hunt planning will only be available on certain quests, including main story quests and the more important side quests, including main story and major side quests in DLC.<br /> <br /> what do you guys think of that?<br /> <br /> EDIT: and of course you would have to manage your terrority, but I am not sure how to go about including that in the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":". 11-01-2015, 10:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T21:25:19-08:00","id":748384,"title":"","content":"From the looks of things Obsidian might be making a video game based in the WoD universe<br /> <br /> That said - I would not mind seeing the WoD MMO game with lots of player created content.<br /> <br /> My 2 cents. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4016-headclot","name":"HeadClot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T14:25:55-08:00","id":750099,"title":"","content":"I still wish they'd do a movie..or maybe another tv show. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T14:44:54-08:00","id":750139,"title":"","content":"Movie or TV is a must. Either as a monster-of-the-week or maybe like the Twilight Zone, OR take a splat, and city and do a supernatural drama/mystery in it. <br /> <br /> On the game side I would absolutely adore to have an open world game with RPG elements. If it's cross-over or not, I will play it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T17:56:30-08:00","id":750361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/743016-speculation-the-future-of-white-wolf-properties-in-other-media?p=745127#post745127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, pipe dream here, but picture an open-world single player game (I imagine Bethesda style, but Ubisoft style would work fine if that's more your cup of tea). You've got your big city sandbox, populated with humans, vampires, werewolves, mages, the works. You start out as a human, and the initial questline has you stumbling into the mysterious and spooky things that walk the city at night. And from there, the sky is the limit. You can play the whole game as a mortal caught up in the machinations of these monsters you just learned existed, take to hunting them, or even become one of them (obviously for splats that are tied to heritage there would have to be a sidequest where you discover your great grandpa was a werewolf, or whatever). Different quests become available or impossible for different splats, so there's a ton of replay value.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Sidenote, I think this would work better set in nWoD, just because nWoD is generally more crossover-friendly, and the modular approach lends itself nicely to sandbox play. But I definitely wouldn't say no to such a game set in oWoD either.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we've all dreamed about that idea at one time or another, but I think there's some serious practical difficulties in getting it to work. I see technical problems with adapting the Obsidian model to a dense open world. Both Fallout and Elder Scrolls are about worlds that are rich with mysteries to discover but sparse of population. There's definitely an issue of how you pack that many characters into a more densely packed urban setting, but I also worry that it undermines one of the core gameplay advantages of the Obsidian model. For me at least, the most addictive appeal of these games is the question of what's over the next hill, and the gameplay loop is predicated on venturing out into the wild and loading yourself down with loot. I'd be concerned that adapting it to a modern day metropolis would strip out a lot of advantages that come from these games and result in a game that shows the seams more readily.<br /> <br /> There's also just the question of practicality regarding budget and manpower. It strikes me that fitting nine different breeds of supernatural into the game and trying to make them distinct would be an overwhelming task, and even if it was possible, the rest of the game would suffer. There would be so much gameplay balance to achieve and balancing all the cross-splat narratives would be a nightmare. I suppose you could simplify things by stripping down the importance of clans/tribes/etc. and reducing it to the core Vampire/Werewolf/Mage model, but even then it would be a pretty ambitious project. And that's not even taking into account managing the distinct politics and morality systems that make each of the game lines unique.<br /> <br /> Maybe the best way to swing it would be to build a game about an individual splat (probably Vampire) and then release DLC expansions for the other splats that are set in the same system? That way you could start with a more approachable model and then use the preexisting market and asset design to create what amounts to pseudo-sequels set within the same model, modular stories that can interact with the status quo of your existing city.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/743016-speculation-the-future-of-white-wolf-properties-in-other-media?p=748234#post748234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My idea of the perfect WtF game would be kinda of like Fallout New Vegas, but with a &quot;hunt planning&quot; feature similar to the preplanning from Payday2 for the more important quests, where you can call in favors from mortals, spirits and other being that you have helped through out the game to help crack the tougher targets of the sacred hunt, by having allies sabotage the enemy defenses, gather intelligence and leave supplies for the pack and other such things.<br /> <br /> and if you play as an Elodoth of the mastermind face, a Rahu of the tactician face or an Irraka of the scout face you get some sort of bonus to preplanning, like help costing fewer favors for the mastermind, or a discount on intelligence for the scout and a discount on more assault style assistance for the tactician. However, calling in favors requires you to help others in order to be owed those favors and some forms of help are only available if specific sorts of people or spirits owe you favors.<br /> <br /> and like I said, to make things manageable for the developers, this detailed hunt planning will only be available on certain quests, including main story quests and the more important side quests, including main story and major side quests in DLC.<br /> <br /> what do you guys think of that?<br /> <br /> EDIT: and of course you would have to manage your terrority, but I am not sure how to go about including that in the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's a neat premise. I loved the heist feature in GTA V, and it sounds like Payday 2 did a solid job with it too.<br /> <br /> I'm not too versed in WtF, but when I think &quot;territory management&quot;, the first thing that comes to mind is State of Decay, a pretty great sandbox zombie game predicated on protecting, scavenging, and defending territory. It could potentially be a great jumping off point for a Werewolf or Hunter game.<br /> <br /> Also, I know it's been done to death, but I think the episodic adventure model Telltale has been following could be adapted to the crossover nature of Vampire pretty adeptly. It could be cool to take a singular city and tangle together narratives from a bunch of splats. The have their own stories that might be loosely, tangentially, or not at all related, but the decisions made in one have ripples across the metropolis' infrastructure and shows how all these vying groups of monsters impact one another even when they've never met.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T17:59:45-08:00","id":750366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaminggod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/743016-speculation-the-future-of-white-wolf-properties-in-other-media?p=750139#post750139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Movie or TV is a must. Either as a monster-of-the-week or maybe like the Twilight Zone, OR take a splat, and city and do a supernatural drama/mystery in it.<br /> <br /> On the game side I would absolutely adore to have an open world game with RPG elements. If it's cross-over or not, I will play it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally down for TV adaptations. I feel like the Vampire and crossover heavy drama angle has been done to death (and I'm bored with the &quot;monster-of-the-week&quot; idea), but I think there's plenty of potential. An anthology series, either with stand-alone episodes a la Twilight Zone and Black Mirror or self-contained seasons like American Horror Story or True Detective could be pretty boss.<br /> <br /> I think there's a lot of potential for long-form narrative television as well, but I'd venture deeper than werewolves and vampire, who already have a pretty extensive market over-saturation. Give me a techgnostic espionage thriller inspired by Demon, a Guillermo Del Toro inspired horror series about changelings on the run from their Fae owners, or a Promethean series inspired by the Incredible Hulk, with a created monster wandering the world, solving the problems of strangers but unable to stay in any place for long.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T04:11:17-08:00","id":751084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaminggod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/743016-speculation-the-future-of-white-wolf-properties-in-other-media?p=750139#post750139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Movie or TV is a must. Either as a monster-of-the-week or maybe like the Twilight Zone, OR take a splat, and city and do a supernatural drama/mystery in it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd love an anthology TV show, where every week we focus on a different supernatural. Sometimes you could do two parters, or sequels to episodes. Or, maybe do the series like American Horror Story or True Detective, where every season is focused on a different stories and characters..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T11:32:13-08:00","id":751873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/743016-speculation-the-future-of-white-wolf-properties-in-other-media?p=751084#post751084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd love an anthology TV show, where every week we focus on a different supernatural. Sometimes you could do two parters, or sequels to episodes. Or, maybe do the series like American Horror Story or True Detective, where every season is focused on a different stories and characters..</div> </div> </div> </div>So, what'd the format be? Twilight Zone? Outerlimits? <br /> <br /> Would the whole set up be a plot where at the end there's a disturbing reveal?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T12:50:59-08:00","id":752066,"title":"","content":"Is there even going to be VtM or WtA in a new &quot;one Wold of Darkness&quot; or are they going the Marvel way and merge nWoD and cWoD into &quot;one World of Darkness&quot; ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T13:02:53-08:00","id":752119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/743016-speculation-the-future-of-white-wolf-properties-in-other-media?p=752066#post752066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there even going to be VtM or WtA in a new &amp;quot;one Wold of Darkness&amp;quot; or are they going the Marvel way and merge nWoD and cWoD into &amp;quot;one World of Darkness&amp;quot; ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh my gods! I hope not. These games need to have their own universe. Doing something like this would destroy them. Please OP, don't let them go this far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T04:15:44-08:00","id":753651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/743016-speculation-the-future-of-white-wolf-properties-in-other-media?p=751873#post751873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, what'd the format be? Twilight Zone? Outerlimits?<br /> <br /> Would the whole set up be a plot where at the end there's a disturbing reveal?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know. My initial idea for an anthology show is more like Twilight Zone or Outer Limits, where every episode is basically a one-off story. Though sometimes you'd revisit characters, do sequels, or crossover with characters from other episodes. That way you could deal with all the WoD has to offer(whether NWoD or CWoD) and not be locked into one thing(though I'll admit True Blood did a pretty decent job of mixing in other supernaturals as the seasons went on).<br /> <br /> But, I don't think having some continuity between episodes and building towards something would be a bad idea either. Maybe have the season(or series) be set in a city, and each episode, while being about different characters(sometimes), builds towards big reveal at the end...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T06:02:20-08:00","id":753812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/743016-speculation-the-future-of-white-wolf-properties-in-other-media?p=750361#post750361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe the best way to swing it would be to build a game about an individual splat (probably Vampire) and then release DLC expansions for the other splats that are set in the same system? That way you could start with a more approachable model and then use the preexisting market and asset design to create what amounts to pseudo-sequels set within the same model, modular stories that can interact with the status quo of your existing city.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is pretty much the way Paradox has handled expansions for CKII. In the base game you could only play feudal Christians and the unplayable faiths and government were kind of shallow, most of the early expansions focused on making the other faiths deeper and playable and added coastal republics as a playable government type. More recent expansions have opened up new areas of the world that were previously handwaved with some scripted events but couldn't be meaningfully interacted with.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/757-filli-noctus","name":"filli noctus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"124"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T17:05:38-08:00","id":755274,"title":"","content":"Hm, what kind of Toyline or models would be made for these games, I wonder? <br /> <br /> If there's ever going to be a move to get them in RPG stores, there's gotta be some for of physical components asside from just RPG books to get them supported. <br /> <br /> I'm thinking atleast some sort of toys or board games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T18:16:22-08:00","id":755466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/743016-speculation-the-future-of-white-wolf-properties-in-other-media?p=755274#post755274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm, what kind of Toyline or models would be made for these games, I wonder? <br /> <br /> If there's ever going to be a move to get them in RPG stores, there's gotta be some for of physical components asside from just RPG books to get them supported. <br /> <br /> I'm thinking atleast some sort of toys or board games.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think there would be that much of a barrier to entry to get in RPG stores. OPP might have been following the POD model for a while, but the WoD brand still holds a lot of cachet.<br /> <br /> I'd be surprised if we don't get strategy board games out of the deal before. Both WW and PI have experience in it.<br /> <br /> As for figures, I'd expect any products to be marketed as premium collectibles. In a world of vampires, werewolves, witches, and frankensteins, the sky's the limit for collectible possibilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}